(634222, 65377, 11843, '<td valign="top">Um, OK! ROFLMAO! I''ll give you a 7 just for the laughs.</td>', 'Um, OK! ROFLMAO! I''ll give you a 7 just for the laughs.', '2004-03-23 22:57:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(634260, 65549, 4494, '<td valign="top">You had me fooled there for a while!   Very creative shot and well done!  Not only the date, but the picture itself should have tipped me off since it''s clearly:)</td>', 'You had me fooled there for a while!   Very creative shot and well done!  Not only the date, but the picture itself should have tipped me off since it''s clearly:)', '2004-03-23 23:19:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(634274, 65401, 18802, '<td valign="top">Really like the action in this. Looks like fun. Shame the background takes so much away from this good picture.</td>', 'Really like the action in this. Looks like fun. Shame the background takes so much away from this good picture.', '2004-03-23 23:41:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(634579, 65459, 15407, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful shot but the magazine has a verticle format not a horizontal format... I''ll bet this would have done excellent in the "Orange" challenge.</td>', 'This is a beautiful shot but the magazine has a verticle format not a horizontal format... I''ll bet this would have done excellent in the "Orange" challenge.', '2004-03-24 01:32:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(634591, 65575, 15407, '<td valign="top">Excellent Photo!  Looks like the dog ate one of my HOT Chili''s!  Isn''t the Dogs magazine a verticle format instead of a horizontal format?</td>', 'Excellent Photo!  Looks like the dog ate one of my HOT Chili''s!  Isn''t the Dogs magazine a verticle format instead of a horizontal format?', '2004-03-24 01:35:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(634602, 65566, 15407, '<td valign="top">Very appropiate subject matter and it has the right tone. The magazine is a verticle format so unlike many of the other photos with a horizontal photo, your''s could be used!</td>', 'Very appropiate subject matter and it has the right tone. The magazine is a verticle format so unlike many of the other photos with a horizontal photo, your''s could be used!', '2004-03-24 01:39:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(634642, 65622, 10848, '<td valign="top">Cute shot, love the orange feet on the front fellow, would have been a good entry for the orange challenge also :) Great clarity and detail.</td>', 'Cute shot, love the orange feet on the front fellow, would have been a good entry for the orange challenge also :) Great clarity and detail.', '2004-03-24 01:51:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(634643, 65737, 10170, '<td valign="top">Beautiful photo, love the DOF, beautiful model.  I was going to use this as a magasine title as well but thought nobody would have heard of it ... but they have :)</td>', 'Beautiful photo, love the DOF, beautiful model.  I was going to use this as a magasine title as well but thought nobody would have heard of it ... but they have :)', '2004-03-24 01:51:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(634646, 65511, 10848, '<td valign="top">Great, good attention to detail the focus on this is wonderful. The color is phenonminal great shot.</td>', 'Great, good attention to detail the focus on this is wonderful. The color is phenonminal great shot.', '2004-03-24 01:52:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(634651, 65459, 10848, '<td valign="top">Only a true artist could execute this beautiful shot, this is a definite wow, how lucky you are that the colors on the wings of the moth are in complete harmony with the colors of the flower. 10</td>', 'Only a true artist could execute this beautiful shot, this is a definite wow, how lucky you are that the colors on the wings of the moth are in complete harmony with the colors of the flower. 10', '2004-03-24 01:55:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(634652, 65209, 15407, '<td valign="top">This is a wonderful photo, although rather ''Zooish''</td>', 'This is a wonderful photo, although rather ''Zooish''', '2004-03-24 01:56:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(634657, 65630, 15407, '<td valign="top">I think the picture would have been better without such a tight crop on the right. Having the tip of the petal on the right would have gained another ''point'' from me. Was it damaged ?</td>', 'I think the picture would have been better without such a tight crop on the right. Having the tip of the petal on the right would have gained another ''point'' from me. Was it damaged ?', '2004-03-24 02:00:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(634672, 65676, 15407, '<td valign="top">An awsome perspective...Though  I noticed that the magazine uses a verticle format for their cover photos''s</td>', 'An awsome perspective...Though  I noticed that the magazine uses a verticle format for their cover photos''s', '2004-03-24 02:07:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(634685, 65834, 15407, '<td valign="top">You did an excellent job on this!  I looked at the magazines and found this not to be the typical type of photo that they use yet I;m sure they would be tempted with this!<br/>I enjoy seeing post processing that brings out the best in a photo!</td>', 'You did an excellent job on this!  I looked at the magazines and found this not to be the typical type of photo that they use yet I;m sure they would be tempted with this!I enjoy seeing post processing that brings out the best in a photo!', '2004-03-24 02:14:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(634686, 65916, 17787, '<td valign="top">Very Beatiful Model and good work!</td>', 'Very Beatiful Model and good work!', '2004-03-24 02:15:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(634692, 65867, 17787, '<td valign="top">Woaow, beatiful girl and very good work!</td>', 'Woaow, beatiful girl and very good work!', '2004-03-24 02:19:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(634693, 65909, 15407, '<td valign="top">Quite a nice photo.  I think that the horizontal format and little negative space would make it difficult to use as a cover shot.</td>', 'Quite a nice photo.  I think that the horizontal format and little negative space would make it difficult to use as a cover shot.', '2004-03-24 02:23:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(634695, 65884, 15407, '<td valign="top">I like this quite a bit. Where is the mountain Goat?  With the sunset (rise?) colors you may have been able to get a little more out of the picture with ''overbakin'' it... One of my favorites!</td>', 'I like this quite a bit. Where is the mountain Goat?  With the sunset (rise?) colors you may have been able to get a little more out of the picture with ''overbakin'' it... One of my favorites!', '2004-03-24 02:31:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(634788, 65765, 15407, '<td valign="top">This is one of my top picks!  I was going to submit one for "Cavallino" but a problem with a neighbor kept me from submitting... This is among my top 3 pick and I think with a little more post processing I would have given it the TOP mark... It probably would have beat any of my choice... in my portfolio...</td>', 'This is one of my top picks!  I was going to submit one for "Cavallino" but a problem with a neighbor kept me from submitting... This is among my top 3 pick and I think with a little more post processing I would have given it the TOP mark... It probably would have beat any of my choice... in my portfolio...', '2004-03-24 03:48:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(634797, 65605, 18552, '<td valign="top">This is a cute shot. To me it would be more effective if the dog were in better focus. The grass seems to be in better focus than the dog. It looks like the dog is smelling the flower.</td>', 'This is a cute shot. To me it would be more effective if the dog were in better focus. The grass seems to be in better focus than the dog. It looks like the dog is smelling the flower.', '2004-03-24 03:53:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(634825, 65327, 18552, '<td valign="top">This is a wonderful flower photo, the focus is great. I think it would be nicer in color. I don''t remember ever seeing a black and white flower on the front of a gardening magazine as one of the main things in flower gardening is color.</td>', 'This is a wonderful flower photo, the focus is great. I think it would be nicer in color. I don''t remember ever seeing a black and white flower on the front of a gardening magazine as one of the main things in flower gardening is color.', '2004-03-24 04:11:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(634830, 65859, 18552, '<td valign="top">What a great shot, looks so much like the pictures on the front of car magazines. If the colors were more saturated and vibrant it would look even more so, I think. All the pictures on the covers of car magazines have such bright colors.</td>', 'What a great shot, looks so much like the pictures on the front of car magazines. If the colors were more saturated and vibrant it would look even more so, I think. All the pictures on the covers of car magazines have such bright colors.', '2004-03-24 04:16:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(634924, 64921, 12674, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, would be nice to see rest of pelllie (I wonder).</td>', 'Nice shot, would be nice to see rest of pelllie (I wonder).', '2004-03-24 05:48:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(634940, 65699, 18213, '<td valign="top">Hún er aðeins of líst en samt náðuru þessu mjög vel. Þessi mynd á allavena vel heima í þessari þemu,,,  Good luck</td>', 'Hún er aðeins of líst en samt náðuru þessu mjög vel. Þessi mynd á allavena vel heima í þessari þemu,,,  Good luck', '2004-03-24 06:16:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(634983, 65561, 6912, '<td valign="top">THE WINNER!</td>', 'THE WINNER!', '2004-03-24 07:06:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(634986, 65700, 6912, '<td valign="top">beautiful perspective, lovely composition and colors! 10 from me</td>', 'beautiful perspective, lovely composition and colors! 10 from me', '2004-03-24 07:07:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(635151, 65700, 6130, '<td valign="top">Nice and good.</td>', 'Nice and good.', '2004-03-24 08:13:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(635316, 65901, 16004, '<td valign="top">I think that if you stood right in front of the train it would have been a bit more exciting (for you as well as the viewer) and the composition might have improved (but obviously not your life expectancy).  I think this is a great shot, and one of the best at fitting the challenge (I can very easily visualise a type face in the top portion of the picture).  Very well done - 9.</td>', 'I think that if you stood right in front of the train it would have been a bit more exciting (for you as well as the viewer) and the composition might have improved (but obviously not your life expectancy).  I think this is a great shot, and one of the best at fitting the challenge (I can very easily visualise a type face in the top portion of the picture).  Very well done - 9.', '2004-03-24 09:00:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(635399, 65606, 18765, '<td valign="top">i think a better background color could have been used.</td>', 'i think a better background color could have been used.', '2004-03-24 09:39:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(635441, 65603, 8522, '<td valign="top">Great subject, I like the reflection. The composition could be improved by not dividing your photo into two vertical halves, it''s a bit of a cliche but I think that rule of thirds could have helped you here.Your subject needs more negative space to look into...  I think you should have stepped back and allowed more space in the left side of the frame.  I also feel that the colours are not saturated enough. The background definitely seems too grey. There is an unfortunate glare in the top-right corner of your subject which detracts a little.</td>', 'Great subject, I like the reflection. The composition could be improved by not dividing your photo into two vertical halves, it''s a bit of a cliche but I think that rule of thirds could have helped you here.Your subject needs more negative space to look into...  I think you should have stepped back and allowed more space in the left side of the frame.  I also feel that the colours are not saturated enough. The background definitely seems too grey. There is an unfortunate glare in the top-right corner of your subject which detracts a little.', '2004-03-24 10:00:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(635447, 65699, 8522, '<td valign="top">Great high-contrast shot, very idiomatic for your chosen magazine. The high-grain effect works nicely here. Not sure about the yellow tint on the lips.  The reflections on the glasses take away from the effect a little for me. Great composition, I like the angle you got looking down on your subject.</td>', 'Great high-contrast shot, very idiomatic for your chosen magazine. The high-grain effect works nicely here. Not sure about the yellow tint on the lips.  The reflections on the glasses take away from the effect a little for me. Great composition, I like the angle you got looking down on your subject.', '2004-03-24 10:03:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(635452, 65893, 8522, '<td valign="top">Photo seems oversharpened, with too much texture and detail in your composition. The eye is not led to your chosen subject of the couple. It seems a bit offputting that they seem to be walking into a dead end... a bit unfortunate for a magazine aimed at older people!</td>', 'Photo seems oversharpened, with too much texture and detail in your composition. The eye is not led to your chosen subject of the couple. It seems a bit offputting that they seem to be walking into a dead end... a bit unfortunate for a magazine aimed at older people!', '2004-03-24 10:06:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(635462, 65408, 8522, '<td valign="top">There are some very interesting elements to this composition, unfortunately the overall effect seems a bit chaotic. The reflections on the floor take away from the shot in my opinion. I think that the eye doen''t have a natural resting place here, and that is what is needed... a focal point.</td>', 'There are some very interesting elements to this composition, unfortunately the overall effect seems a bit chaotic. The reflections on the floor take away from the shot in my opinion. I think that the eye doen''t have a natural resting place here, and that is what is needed... a focal point.', '2004-03-24 10:10:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(635468, 65857, 8522, '<td valign="top">Nice level of detail in the foreground, but I think you needed greater depth of field. The foreground water seems a bit overexposed... if you haven''t already I would decrease the contrast levels in your camera so you can capture a greater dynamic range and increase the contrast back in Photoshop. The composition seems to lead the eye out of the shot, which is not a good thing here. The eye should be led to a point somewhere in the picture, preferably at one of the thirds junctions. Not quite sure why you went for a sepia look here. The trees in the background take away from your composition. Not sure what you wanted to achieve here in general.</td>', 'Nice level of detail in the foreground, but I think you needed greater depth of field. The foreground water seems a bit overexposed... if you haven''t already I would decrease the contrast levels in your camera so you can capture a greater dynamic range and increase the contrast back in Photoshop. The composition seems to lead the eye out of the shot, which is not a good thing here. The eye should be led to a point somewhere in the picture, preferably at one of the thirds junctions. Not quite sure why you went for a sepia look here. The trees in the background take away from your composition. Not sure what you wanted to achieve here in general.', '2004-03-24 10:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(635473, 65867, 8522, '<td valign="top">Wow, a stunning shot. Excellent model, great attitude. Very effective in b&amp;w. Composition is excellent, I love the tilt of the head and the placement of the hands. Great use of water. The hair looks fantastic. Imaginative and effective crop. Only criticism is that in my opinion it is a little overexposed. This may have been intentional, but the effect doesn''t quite work for me.</td>', 'Wow, a stunning shot. Excellent model, great attitude. Very effective in b&w. Composition is excellent, I love the tilt of the head and the placement of the hands. Great use of water. The hair looks fantastic. Imaginative and effective crop. Only criticism is that in my opinion it is a little overexposed. This may have been intentional, but the effect doesn''t quite work for me.', '2004-03-24 10:17:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(635475, 65901, 8522, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, great composition for a magazine cover. However, there seems to be too much detail in the shot, I would prefer more simplicity... there''s just too much for the eye to look at which leads the eye away from your train. The light seems a little harsh, and it''s unfortunate that shadows obscure a lot of the detail at the front of the train.</td>', 'Nice shot, great composition for a magazine cover. However, there seems to be too much detail in the shot, I would prefer more simplicity... there''s just too much for the eye to look at which leads the eye away from your train. The light seems a little harsh, and it''s unfortunate that shadows obscure a lot of the detail at the front of the train.', '2004-03-24 10:22:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(635480, 65826, 8522, '<td valign="top">Photo seems okay, but doesn''t really grab me. A couple of things bother me... you need more depth of field, the signs in the background are blurred. And the vertical writing in the left of the frame distracts me as it looks like it has been unintentionally chopped in half. The arrows in your shot could have been used as a composition device to lead the eye to something of interest, but that doesn''t really happen here.</td>', 'Photo seems okay, but doesn''t really grab me. A couple of things bother me... you need more depth of field, the signs in the background are blurred. And the vertical writing in the left of the frame distracts me as it looks like it has been unintentionally chopped in half. The arrows in your shot could have been used as a composition device to lead the eye to something of interest, but that doesn''t really happen here.', '2004-03-24 10:25:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(635489, 65466, 8522, '<td valign="top">Very interesting composition, which invites the viewer to reflect on it for a while. Subtle and imaginative use of blue and red. Not sure what happened to your foreground texture though, it doesn''t look good up close. Is this as a result of butchery by NeatImage? Maybe too much contrast? I would say that the overall mood, although very effective, is too drab and bleak for a tourism magazine.</td>', 'Very interesting composition, which invites the viewer to reflect on it for a while. Subtle and imaginative use of blue and red. Not sure what happened to your foreground texture though, it doesn''t look good up close. Is this as a result of butchery by NeatImage? Maybe too much contrast? I would say that the overall mood, although very effective, is too drab and bleak for a tourism magazine.', '2004-03-24 10:30:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(635492, 65397, 8522, '<td valign="top">Shot seems to much like a snapshot. Too overexposed. The composition is not effective, it looks like the photographer wanted more of the gondola in the shot and misfired. The gondolier''s face is obscured by his arm. The couple in the gondola are not interesting and look bored. The background does not look like it has been thought about.</td>', 'Shot seems to much like a snapshot. Too overexposed. The composition is not effective, it looks like the photographer wanted more of the gondola in the shot and misfired. The gondolier''s face is obscured by his arm. The couple in the gondola are not interesting and look bored. The background does not look like it has been thought about.', '2004-03-24 10:33:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(635496, 65853, 8522, '<td valign="top">Very cute... a little overexposed though, especially on his face where you have blown-out highlights. The rest of him could do with darkening so you can see more of the textures in the feathers.  The whiteish foliage to his right in the background detracts a little, and the shadow detracts a lot. I think negative space is always needed in the direction that a person or animal is looking into. Here, you need more negative space to the left of the shot to give him room to look into.</td>', 'Very cute... a little overexposed though, especially on his face where you have blown-out highlights. The rest of him could do with darkening so you can see more of the textures in the feathers.  The whiteish foliage to his right in the background detracts a little, and the shadow detracts a lot. I think negative space is always needed in the direction that a person or animal is looking into. Here, you need more negative space to the left of the shot to give him room to look into.', '2004-03-24 10:37:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(635501, 65634, 8522, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, I like the motion blur. Shame you can see the background, it would have worked a lot better if the background was completely black. I would also have liked to see more of the acrobat''s face.</td>', 'Nice shot, I like the motion blur. Shame you can see the background, it would have worked a lot better if the background was completely black. I would also have liked to see more of the acrobat''s face.', '2004-03-24 10:40:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(635607, 64921, 6008, '<td valign="top">It''s a good shot with plenty of room for title and blurbs. Exposure and color is good on the bird, but it could have done with a tad more sharpness.</td>', 'It''s a good shot with plenty of room for title and blurbs. Exposure and color is good on the bird, but it could have done with a tad more sharpness.', '2004-03-24 11:46:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(635618, 65327, 6008, '<td valign="top">It''s a good shot with nice details on the petals and stamen. Could have done with a little more contrast as a black and white image. Like I said, it''s a good shot, but I think for a flower to be able to carry off black and white, especially for a magazine cover, it needs to be absolutely stunning. Black and white flowers tend to be classy and/or moody, and I would expect a lot more vibrant color from a magazine cover. As a side note, I''m not voting you down for it at all, it''s merely an observation.</td>', 'It''s a good shot with nice details on the petals and stamen. Could have done with a little more contrast as a black and white image. Like I said, it''s a good shot, but I think for a flower to be able to carry off black and white, especially for a magazine cover, it needs to be absolutely stunning. Black and white flowers tend to be classy and/or moody, and I would expect a lot more vibrant color from a magazine cover. As a side note, I''m not voting you down for it at all, it''s merely an observation.', '2004-03-24 11:51:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(635623, 65655, 6008, '<td valign="top">The composition and subject is certainly something you''d expect to see on a magazine, with plenty of room for the title as well. As for the image itself, I find it soft, probably as a result of being handheld.</td>', 'The composition and subject is certainly something you''d expect to see on a magazine, with plenty of room for the title as well. As for the image itself, I find it soft, probably as a result of being handheld.', '2004-03-24 11:53:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(635626, 65910, 6008, '<td valign="top">Nice blue sky, fairly sharp, standard composition with plenty of room for title and blurbs. I could see this working well for a magazine cover.</td>', 'Nice blue sky, fairly sharp, standard composition with plenty of room for title and blurbs. I could see this working well for a magazine cover.', '2004-03-24 11:55:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(635634, 65826, 6008, '<td valign="top">I dont know this magazine so not sure if this is the standard thing in there. As an image it''s a good blend of architecture and local interest. Bordering on too many elements, and as shot there wouldnt be much room to add title or blurbs without adding to the chaos, although I''m sure a magazine layout editor could do something with it. Good blend of colors, the details are not too bad, and the exposure is good.</td>', 'I dont know this magazine so not sure if this is the standard thing in there. As an image it''s a good blend of architecture and local interest. Bordering on too many elements, and as shot there wouldnt be much room to add title or blurbs without adding to the chaos, although I''m sure a magazine layout editor could do something with it. Good blend of colors, the details are not too bad, and the exposure is good.', '2004-03-24 11:59:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(635641, 65474, 6008, '<td valign="top">Obviously the first thing to see is that it is shot in landscape mode, but I''m sure a magazine layout editor could do something with it. The image is seasonal, slightly amusing, and could cover a topic about pets in winter or similar so I could see it on the front of the magazine. It''s a tad soft, and the eyes are a little dark, which is disappointing as they seem to be my main focus due to the expression. A little dodging on the eyes could bring out the catchlight a little more and make them more pronounced.</td>', 'Obviously the first thing to see is that it is shot in landscape mode, but I''m sure a magazine layout editor could do something with it. The image is seasonal, slightly amusing, and could cover a topic about pets in winter or similar so I could see it on the front of the magazine. It''s a tad soft, and the eyes are a little dark, which is disappointing as they seem to be my main focus due to the expression. A little dodging on the eyes could bring out the catchlight a little more and make them more pronounced.', '2004-03-24 12:02:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(635650, 65857, 6008, '<td valign="top">First off I''m not familiar with this magazine so no idea what is normally on the cover or the subjects they write about. Secondly, the use of landscape mode, which I''m sure a magazine layout editor could still use but the composition does suggest a strong wide angle. I personally dont find much interest in the subject presented, but that''s not to say that other people wouldnt either. I dont know the limitations you had while shooting, but as a suggestion - it may have been interesting to get a single tunnel/arch thingie and concentrated on that with the water coming through.</td>', 'First off I''m not familiar with this magazine so no idea what is normally on the cover or the subjects they write about. Secondly, the use of landscape mode, which I''m sure a magazine layout editor could still use but the composition does suggest a strong wide angle. I personally dont find much interest in the subject presented, but that''s not to say that other people wouldnt either. I dont know the limitations you had while shooting, but as a suggestion - it may have been interesting to get a single tunnel/arch thingie and concentrated on that with the water coming through.', '2004-03-24 12:07:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(635656, 65893, 10644, '<td valign="top">i think this would be great on aarp</td>', 'i think this would be great on aarp', '2004-03-24 12:09:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(635658, 65676, 10644, '<td valign="top">what a perspective</td>', 'what a perspective', '2004-03-24 12:09:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(635660, 65777, 10644, '<td valign="top">beautiful</td>', 'beautiful', '2004-03-24 12:09:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(635661, 65460, 10644, '<td valign="top">incredible clarity and dof</td>', 'incredible clarity and dof', '2004-03-24 12:10:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(635666, 65776, 6008, '<td valign="top">Good composition and good color. Using the background to promote the potential background of the wine is nicely done and presents a story more than just a product shot. Plenty of space for title and blurbs. I''m not sure the second glass needed to be in the shot and find the rim just a tad distracting and it probably adds to the reflections in the glass. The reflections dont show or suggest anything unnatural, so that''s good too!</td>', 'Good composition and good color. Using the background to promote the potential background of the wine is nicely done and presents a story more than just a product shot. Plenty of space for title and blurbs. I''m not sure the second glass needed to be in the shot and find the rim just a tad distracting and it probably adds to the reflections in the glass. The reflections dont show or suggest anything unnatural, so that''s good too!', '2004-03-24 12:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(635667, 65209, 10644, '<td valign="top">gorgeous detail</td>', 'gorgeous detail', '2004-03-24 12:11:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(635668, 65634, 10644, '<td valign="top">very nice</td>', 'very nice', '2004-03-24 12:11:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(635670, 65916, 10644, '<td valign="top">nice lighting</td>', 'nice lighting', '2004-03-24 12:12:09.000000', NULL, 1),
