(642043, 65622, 772, '<td valign="top">Hi Lorrie...<br/> <br/>I was just reading your comment about the light not being good because it was overcast.  I found that quite interesting because I do a lot of duck/geese/waterfowl photos and I generally prefer overcast skies to direct sunlight for them.  I find my good exposures come a lot easier in even soft light rather than harsh sun.  This particular image could have had some rough shadows underneath or on either side with direct sun... I just thought I would toss that in here and see how u felt about it.  :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Hi Lorrie... I was just reading your comment about the light not being good because it was overcast.  I found that quite interesting because I do a lot of duck/geese/waterfowl photos and I generally prefer overcast skies to direct sunlight for them.  I find my good exposures come a lot easier in even soft light rather than harsh sun.  This particular image could have had some rough shadows underneath or on either side with direct sun... I just thought I would toss that in here and see how u felt about it.  :) John Setzler', '2004-03-29 01:59:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(642048, 65700, 772, '<td valign="top">Jon, this was one of my favorite photos in the challenge, but I never got around to commenting on much this week.  This is an excellent photo.  I love the angry feel of the clouds.  The color here is nice but I''m wondering if you have experimented with a slightly contrasty and grainy b/w feel for this one...<br/> <br/>Nice work :)</td>', 'Jon, this was one of my favorite photos in the challenge, but I never got around to commenting on much this week.  This is an excellent photo.  I love the angry feel of the clouds.  The color here is nice but I''m wondering if you have experimented with a slightly contrasty and grainy b/w feel for this one... Nice work :)', '2004-03-29 02:01:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(642051, 65866, 7350, '<td valign="top">Fantastic perspective!  This gives her that "big head" look.  Her eyes are well captured, and the background nicely blurred.  What really does it for me is the bare feet.  Fantastic shot!</td>', 'Fantastic perspective!  This gives her that "big head" look.  Her eyes are well captured, and the background nicely blurred.  What really does it for me is the bare feet.  Fantastic shot!', '2004-03-29 02:03:07.000000', NULL, 0),
