(644399, 65749, 6870, '<td valign="top">I liked this one, Steve. The colors are so nice, and the clarity is so good, as with most of your photos. It might be good to find a flower without so much debris on it, though. Keep up the good work!</td>', 'I liked this one, Steve. The colors are so nice, and the clarity is so good, as with most of your photos. It might be good to find a flower without so much debris on it, though. Keep up the good work!', '2004-03-30 20:46:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(644400, 65630, 13390, '<td valign="top"><b>*From the Critique Club*</b> <br/> <br/>I am looking forward to critiquing this shot. It may be hard though because this is quite a good shot.  ;)<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/> <br/>This is generally the area where I am most picky, but I would have to agree with what Rasai said in the fact that the crop was a bit tight, that was the first thing that came to my mind when I saw the shot. It is not a bad thing, but it is one of those things that can make a difference between an extremely good shot and a WOW shot. One other real nit-picky thing is I feel the flower is a tad bit centered in the shot (The direction of the petals saves this from being to big of a problem because they lead the eyes quite well, also, another thing that saves that is the yellow area which is nicely placed). Now, I am not saying these things to make you feel bad about the composition; I am just saying things that <i>I</i> think would help make this shot stellar.There are a lot of good compostional things in this photo, and like I mentioned before they are the petals and the yellow center of the trillium. Oh, and more more thin, I was NOT a stickler about the format of these shots, but you made a wise decision to make it vertical because that''s what the voters were looking for apparently.<br/> <br/><b>Color and Lighting:</b> <br/> <br/>I really like the lighting in this shot, probably the strongest element in the shot. You highlighted the petals and yellow center just right to ad extra emphasis on the flower. The colors work really well because the sharp yellow and white area of the flower contrast real nicely with the duller green background.<br/> <br/><b>Focus and Depth of Field:</b> <br/> <br/>The focus here quite good. I see that you have used NeatImage on this shot. It is nice to see that you spent time to get the desired effect without losing too much quality, like at all, I appreciate that a lot! I do feel that the DOF field could be slighly more shallow to add even more emphasis to your trillium. The sharpness of the one green leaf slightly detracts.<br/> <br/><b>Other Thoughts:</b> <br/> <br/>Overall, very nicely done. There was just a few minor things that kind of held you back from being a STELLAR WOW kind of shot. Good clarity, lighting, and color play a huge role in your 6 score.<br/> <br/>~Matthew Dykman (goinskiing)<br/> <br/>If you have any comments questions or concerns, feel free to PM me at any time.</td>', '*From the Critique Club*  I am looking forward to critiquing this shot. It may be hard though because this is quite a good shot.  ;) Composition:  This is generally the area where I am most picky, but I would have to agree with what Rasai said in the fact that the crop was a bit tight, that was the first thing that came to my mind when I saw the shot. It is not a bad thing, but it is one of those things that can make a difference between an extremely good shot and a WOW shot. One other real nit-picky thing is I feel the flower is a tad bit centered in the shot (The direction of the petals saves this from being to big of a problem because they lead the eyes quite well, also, another thing that saves that is the yellow area which is nicely placed). Now, I am not saying these things to make you feel bad about the composition; I am just saying things that I think would help make this shot stellar.There are a lot of good compostional things in this photo, and like I mentioned before they are the petals and the yellow center of the trillium. Oh, and more more thin, I was NOT a stickler about the format of these shots, but you made a wise decision to make it vertical because that''s what the voters were looking for apparently. Color and Lighting:  I really like the lighting in this shot, probably the strongest element in the shot. You highlighted the petals and yellow center just right to ad extra emphasis on the flower. The colors work really well because the sharp yellow and white area of the flower contrast real nicely with the duller green background. Focus and Depth of Field:  The focus here quite good. I see that you have used NeatImage on this shot. It is nice to see that you spent time to get the desired effect without losing too much quality, like at all, I appreciate that a lot! I do feel that the DOF field could be slighly more shallow to add even more emphasis to your trillium. The sharpness of the one green leaf slightly detracts. Other Thoughts:  Overall, very nicely done. There was just a few minor things that kind of held you back from being a STELLAR WOW kind of shot. Good clarity, lighting, and color play a huge role in your 6 score. ~Matthew Dykman (goinskiing) If you have any comments questions or concerns, feel free to PM me at any time.', '2004-03-30 20:50:27.000000', NULL, 0),
